{"instance_id": "SpikeInterface__spikeinterface-2775", "repo": "SpikeInterface/spikeinterface", "base_commit": "c6f8f1fae2ed8fa80b59c42cf8d1cff523b3c754", "image_name": "swerebench/sweb.eval.x86_64.spikeinterface_1776_spikeinterface-2775", "docker_image": "swerebench/sweb.eval.x86_64.spikeinterface_1776_spikeinterface-2775", "problem_statement": "Split function and `new_unit_ids` definition\nHi !\r\n\r\nI was looking into the curation module and didn't quite get how to use the split function. Let's say I want to split my unit into 3. To do so I just have to properly define my `indices_list` and then I could just do as so:\r\n`cs.split(unit_id, indices_list)`\r\n\r\nThe class `SplitUnitSorting` is able to handle this, thanks to `tot_splits = max([v.max() for v in indices_list]) + 1`. \r\nBut then we are asserting `assert len(new_unit_ids) <= tot_splits`, and `new_unit_ids` is defined in the `CurationSorting` class :\r\n```\r\nnew_unit_ids = self._get_unused_id(2)\r\n        new_sorting = SplitUnitSorting(\r\n            current_sorting,\r\n            split_unit_id=split_unit_id,\r\n            indices_list=indices_list,\r\n            new_unit_ids=new_unit_ids,\r\n            properties_policy=self._properties_policy,\r\n        )\r\n```\r\nTherefore even if do properly my list, there will always be only 2 `new_unit_ids`.\r\n\r\nWould solve it doing `new_unit_ids = self._get_unused_id(max(np.unique(indices_list)))` but I am not sure weither this should be changed or if I am not doing it the proper way.\r\n\r\nThanks !", "FAIL_TO_PASS": ["src/spikeinterface/curation/tests/test_curationsorting.py::test_curation"], "PASS_TO_PASS": ["src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeRandomSpikes[False-memory]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeRandomSpikes[False-binary_folder]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeRandomSpikes[False-zarr]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeWaveforms[True-memory]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeWaveforms[True-binary_folder]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeWaveforms[True-zarr]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeWaveforms[False-memory]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeWaveforms[False-binary_folder]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeWaveforms[False-zarr]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeTemplates[True-memory]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeTemplates[True-binary_folder]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeTemplates[True-zarr]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeTemplates[False-memory]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeTemplates[False-binary_folder]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeTemplates[False-zarr]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeNoiseLevels[True-memory]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeNoiseLevels[True-binary_folder]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeNoiseLevels[True-zarr]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeNoiseLevels[False-memory]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeNoiseLevels[False-binary_folder]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_ComputeNoiseLevels[False-zarr]", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_core.py::test_get_children_dependencies", "src/spikeinterface/core/tests/test_analyzer_extension_co